# ArduCopter guided-mode speed/acceleration/jerk limits for car tracking.
#
# GUIDED velocity control (what relative_position_controller sends via
# /mavros/setpoint_velocity/cmd_vel) takes its horizontal limits from the
# waypoint-navigation parameters (ModeGuided::pva_control_start):
#   WP_SPD  default 10 m/s
#   WP_ACC  default 2.5 m/s^2
#
# With the default hold_location shot (18 m to the side), a car turning at
# ~16 deg/s at 5 m/s moves the shot point at ~10 m/s on a ~36 m circle, which
# needs ~2.9 m/s^2 just to stay on the curve: more than the defaults allow,
# so the drone fell 30-70 m behind (run 20260924_151933, t >= 370 s).
#
# WP_ACC 5 stays inside what the default 30 deg lean limit (ATC_ANGLE_MAX) can
# give: 9.81 * tan(30 deg) = 5.7 m/s^2. Keep pid_max_speed_xy <= WP_SPD and
# pid_max_accel_xy == WP_ACC in relative_position_controller.
#
# PSC_NE_JERK is left at its default (5 m/s^3). Raising it to 20 (run
# 20260924_161755) did not shorten the ~1.2 s command->velocity delay, which is
# mostly the vehicle following its own target (attitude/velocity loops), and it
# removed smoothing that damped the position loop: the drone then oscillated
# +-6 m sideways even with the car parked.
#
# If a change here seems to have no effect, SITL is using a value saved in
# ~/ardupilot/eeprom.bin: start sim_vehicle.py once with -w to wipe it.

WP_SPD       15
WP_ACC       5
